<title>UK: Scottish Hydro ease on Goldman downgrading.</title>
<headline>Scottish Hydro ease on Goldman downgrading.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Scottish Hydro-Electric Plc eased on Friday as brokerage Goldman Sachs cuts the utility from &quot;market performer&quot; to &quot;underperformer&quot;, dealers said</p>
<p>By 0915 GMT the stock was down 5-1/2p to 419-1/2p. On Thursday it surged to a new year high following good figures for the financial year 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;This comes on the back of the recent price move&quot;, a trader said.</p>
<p>An analyst at Goldman was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
